                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0902e72e-7667-4c59-9a4e-478e7283c791",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "concentred"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ea343252-a1b3-40f5-ac97-2232dc50ba86",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "concentred"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d19113c4-2681-3a60-98c8-dc1df31127ef",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To come together at a common centre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7b5b677-a5b6-475f-833e-9e3b1c48ba4d",
                                "sense_id": "d19113c4-2681-3a60-98c8-dc1df31127ef",
                                "text": "As from each angle of the Vault / Wherein thou lyeſt, a line is brought / Vnto the Kingly founders heart; / So vnto thee, from euery part, / See how our loues doe runne by line, / And dead, concenter in thy Shrine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4b2149d-72b3-4a56-8055-58afb8a36720",
                                "sense_id": "d19113c4-2681-3a60-98c8-dc1df31127ef",
                                "text": "Hence, […] whatsoever perfections or properties (except such as are purely personal) are attributed to any of these divine Persons, are the same in all, and may equally be attributed to every one; they being all and every one the same God, in whom all perfections concentre, or, rather, who is all perfection itself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad76eac6-5642-46f1-aec8-be12040555ed",
                                "sense_id": "d19113c4-2681-3a60-98c8-dc1df31127ef",
                                "text": "[T]he medulla oblongata, wherein it was generally agreed by Dutch anatomiſts, that all the minute nerves from all the organs of the ſeven ſenſes concentered, like ſtreets and winding alleys, into a ſquare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4ea4f97-7612-4591-9151-78cf63aa4173",
                                "sense_id": "d19113c4-2681-3a60-98c8-dc1df31127ef",
                                "text": "Capt. Lewis walked on Shore above this Creek and discovered a high moun from the top of which he had an extensive view, 3 paths Concentering at the moun"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10b9186d-ca2f-3e25-826f-c50d0f6fc91b",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To coincide."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e654ac22-f8b9-4fdb-ba4d-67222a09bbc6",
                                "sense_id": "10b9186d-ca2f-3e25-826f-c50d0f6fc91b",
                                "text": "Are we not ſufficiently Brutes, to call that work brutiſh which begets us? […] All Opinions concenter in this, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67b9f3c9-638c-3b72-a0e3-5c784014a4f3",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bring together at a common centre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20832a09-a86f-407f-9072-5b027c48b09e",
                                "sense_id": "67b9f3c9-638c-3b72-a0e3-5c784014a4f3",
                                "text": "For one ſo rarely tun’d to fit all parts; / For one to whom eſpous’d are all the Arts; / Long have I ſought for: but co’d never ſee / Them all concenter’d in one man, but Thee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7169981-3a95-443c-9611-2d583cc6861f",
                                "sense_id": "67b9f3c9-638c-3b72-a0e3-5c784014a4f3",
                                "text": "[T]hir bright officious Lamps, / Light above Light, for thee alone, as ſeems, / In thee concentring all thir precious beams / Of ſacred influence: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "badbd019-6237-4936-85a9-ca0c5fd6d2fc",
                                "sense_id": "67b9f3c9-638c-3b72-a0e3-5c784014a4f3",
                                "text": "Whatever has diſtinguiſhed the hero; whatever has elevated the wit; whatever has endeared the lover, are all concentered in Mr Frolick; whoſe life has, for ſeven years, been a regular interchange of intrigues, dangers, waggeries; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17aee2d1-8bc3-4fe7-b20d-0393b8ebf4b1",
                                "sense_id": "67b9f3c9-638c-3b72-a0e3-5c784014a4f3",
                                "text": "[…] for he never on any occaſion diſplayed his ſenſibility to mortifications, which was in proportion to his exceſſive vanity, but concentred within his vindictive ſoul his diſgrace, his reſentment, and his projects of vengeance."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ba29508-53fd-32e2-a316-3fdb6749fff0",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To focus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a1afe43-fad7-4a2a-b4cd-1c7c5233c6f4",
                                "sense_id": "5ba29508-53fd-32e2-a316-3fdb6749fff0",
                                "text": "At Princess Paryli’s Ball two young men of singular elegance were observed by Diana, little though she concentered her attention on any figures of the groups."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ea7c703-ac2e-456f-9347-28a86cd2147d",
                                "sense_id": "5ba29508-53fd-32e2-a316-3fdb6749fff0",
                                "text": "For an instant the gaze of the horror-stricken multitude was concentred on the ghastly miracle; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a737a89-630f-4d3d-b31e-bb0aa609f9b4",
                                "sense_id": "5ba29508-53fd-32e2-a316-3fdb6749fff0",
                                "text": "Education has been concentred on intellectual (and physical) development; but the affections have been left to take care of themselves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1fca763-7742-3977-b46b-258229ec87c6",
                        "entry_id": "1b90eccb-865e-3e7e-87d3-c4f618341823",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To condense, to concentrate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b13d8c6-ea89-4653-941e-bce170766228",
                                "sense_id": "f1fca763-7742-3977-b46b-258229ec87c6",
                                "text": "Breathes there the man, with soul so dead, / Who never to himself hath said, / This is my own, my native land! […] The wretch, concentered all in self, / Living, shall forfeit fair renown, / And, doubly dying, shall go down / To the vile dust, from whence he sprung, / Unwept, unhonoured, and unsung."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "587b6537-ecdc-40a8-abdd-047ffea6f5fe",
                                "sense_id": "f1fca763-7742-3977-b46b-258229ec87c6",
                                "text": "Ah, I wish you were of my humble temper: the more we limit and concentre happiness, the more certain, I think, we are of securing it—they who widen the circle, encroach upon the boundaries of danger; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a26f396-3a90-4e69-848b-6dcbfea466e2",
                                "sense_id": "f1fca763-7742-3977-b46b-258229ec87c6",
                                "text": "As new discoveries were made incidental difficulties connected with the filling of shells occupied the concentered study of the manufacturers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
